# Rust / Tauri runtime configuration. Copy to .env for local development.
# dotenvy searches the process working directory and its parents, NOT the binary
# directory. Existing process environment variables take precedence.
# A packaged app does not embed this file: provide environment variables through
# its launcher or place .env in the working directory used to launch the app.
# REQUIRED means set explicitly; NOT REQUIRED means the default is sufficient.

# NOT REQUIRED locally: default http://localhost:8081.
# REQUIRED for remote production: set the public HTTPS PowerSync endpoint.
# POWERSYNC_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8081

# NOT REQUIRED locally: default http://localhost:8090.
# REQUIRED for remote production: set the public HTTPS backend base URL.
# Rust uses this for POST /api/sync/upload. Match Angular's build-time apiBaseUrl
# in ../src/environments/environment.prod.ts; this variable does not change it.
# API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8090

# Sync uses the backend JWT obtained at login and stored in the OS keyring.
# No dev token, JWT_SECRET, DB credentials or PowerSync admin token belong here.
